-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Half of Europe witnessed record heat stress this summer — EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a5ccfb19427d746989d61ec6a2b0cce5fa43c378fa4dc148ea5f5c4f8743f00</id><updated>2026-10-03T05:28:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/half-of-europe-witnessed-record-heat-stress-this-summer-eu/a-79514799--b11552623347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/half-of-europe-witnessed-record-heat-stress-this-summer-eu/a-79514799?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's climate monitor said this summer was third-warmest for the continent on record. European rivers also registered their lowest average flows since records began in 1992.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
